  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dominican-Republic guitar-based bolero-derivative couple-dance romantic-song tradition originated 1960s in Santo-Domingo-and-Cibao rural-and-urban barrios. The ensemble: requinto lead-guitar (small-bodied higher-pitched playing arpeggio-and-melodic-fills), segunda rhythm-guitar (six-string playing strum-pattern with güira metallic-scraper), bongos, and bajo electric-bass. The bachata-clave 4-beat pattern emphasizes the second-and-fourth beats with bongo accents. Five historical phases: 1960s-foundational (acoustic-guitar bolero-rural-rhythm), 1970s-marginalized (urban-poor barrio-association), 1980s-electrified (electric-instruments incorporation), 1990s-mainstreamed (bachata-rosa commercial-crossover), and 2000s-onward modern-bachata (urban-bachata fusion with R&B and reggaeton).",
